%N A037589 Decimal expansion of a(n) is given by the first n terms of the periodic sequence with initial period 3,1.
%H A037589 <a href="/index/Rec#order_03">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (10,1,-10).
%F A037589 G.f.: x*(3+x)/((1-x)*(1+x)*(1-10*x)). - _Jaume Oliver Lafont_, Mar 24 2009
%F A037589 From _Elmo R. Oliveira_, Sep 07 2026: (Start)
%F A037589 a(n) = 10*a(n-1) + a(n-2) - 10*a(n-3).
%F A037589 a(n) = floor((31/99)*10^n) = (31*10^n - 9*(-1)^n - 22)/99.
%F A037589 E.g.f.: (31*(exp(10*x) - cosh(x)) - 13*sinh(x))/99. (End)
%t A037589 Table[FromDigits[PadRight[{},n,{3,1}]],{n,22}] (* _Harvey P. Dale_, Oct 19 2016 *)
